The CLR implements generics via type erasure for reference types and code specialization for value types, balancing flexibility and efficiency. This means that generic code is compiled to IL, which is then executed by the CLR. Type erasure ensures that generic code can work with any type, while code specialization optimizes performance by generating specialized code for value types.

