{
    var data = GetDataFromWebServiceAsync();
    ProcessData(data);
}
```
In this example, the `ProcessDataAsync` method is declared with the async keyword, but we forget to use the `await` keyword when calling the `GetDataFromWebServiceAsync` method. This means that the `ProcessData` method will be called before the data is retrieved, which can lead to unexpected behavior and errors.

